From cddb764c791bf5f6e14a8bec84d3a0d86e6ad7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chhowm <chhowm@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:53:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Crop vision detection to each ROI and keep counting late
 detections as input in the tracker

Vision handed the whole 1280x800 frame to detect for every ROI, so one
frame took 160 ms on the site laptop. process_frame now passes only the
ROI bounding box plus 64 px and shifts the blobs back; results match the
full-frame call and the real site frame takes 28.5 ms.

The tracker dropped detections older than t_state without counting them as
received, so once an input gap let the empty-frame timer move t_state to
wall time, detections arriving 0.3 s late were dropped forever.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
